# Board tracking (required)

Every distinct work item (feature, bug, enhancement, research, refactor) **must** exist as a card in `.devtool/features/` before implementation starts. This is not optional for “small” code or docs changes.

## Before coding

1. Scan `.devtool/features/` and `done/` for an existing card (match title/intent).
2. If none: create one (`todo` if the user asked to do it now, else `backlog`). Then set `in-progress` when you start.
3. If one exists: set `in-progress`, update `modified`. Do not duplicate.
4. One card per work item. Split only when the user asks for separate tracks.

## During / after

- Ready to verify: `review`. Finished: `done`, set `completedAt`, move to `.devtool/features/done/`.
- If the request grows, add cards for the extra items (do not leave them only in chat).

## Skip only when

- Question/explanation with no repo change, **or**
- User explicitly says not to put it on the board.

Card format and ID rules: follow `.cursor/skills/kanban-markdown/SKILL.md`.
